NAME
     xargs - build command lines from standard input

SYNOPSIS
     xargs [-0] [-r] [-t] [-p] [-n MAX] [-L N] [-I STR] [-s SIZE] [COMMAND...]

DESCRIPTION
     xargs reads words from standard input and runs COMMAND (echo by
     default) with them appended, as many at a time as will fit.

OPTIONS
     -0        input is separated by null bytes, not whitespace
     -r        do not run the command at all if there is no input
     -t        print each command line before running it
     -p        ask before each one
     -n MAX    at most MAX arguments per run
     -L N      one run per N lines of input
     -I STR    replace STR in the command with the line
     -s SIZE   at most SIZE bytes per command line

SEE ALSO
     find(1), sh(1)
